WEBVTT

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.240
Where are you going?
Don't leave me alone

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.080
How do I follow you

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:25.320
-Into the unknown?
-(ANGELIC VOICE VOCALIZES)

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.440
(GASPS)

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.080
(GASPS)

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.280
Air, fire, water, earth.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.440
(GASPS)

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.520
(ALL EXCLAIMING)

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.160
(ALL GASP)

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.160
(ALL EXCLAIM)

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.080
WOMAN: The water!

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.240
(WIND GUSTING)

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.240
(PANTING)

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.160
The air rages,
no fire, no water.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.640
The earth is next.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:11.920
We have to get out.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.680
(PEOPLE WHIMPERING)

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.040
(CLAMORING)

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.240
It'll be okay.
Evacuate to the cliffs.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.200
(GRUNTS)

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.680
Oh, no!
I'm gonna blow!

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.280
I've got you!

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.640
KRISTOFF: Yes.
Everyone's out and safe.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.280
-Here. Take one of these.
-SVEN: Huh?

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.520
You okay there, Olaf?

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.600
Oh, yeah.
We're calling this...

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.920
"controlling what you can when
things feel out of control."

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.600
Okay, I don't understand.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.280
You've been hearing a voice

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.160
and you didn't think
to tell me?

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.440
I didn't want to worry you.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.360
We made a promise
not to shut each other out.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.240
Just tell me what's going on.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.960
I woke the magical spirits
at the Enchanted Forest.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.680
Okay, that's definitely not

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.120
what I thought
you were gonna say.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.840
Wait. The Enchanted Forest?

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.640
The one
Father warned us about?

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.720
Yes.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.080
Why would you do that?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.600
Because of the voice.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.520
I know it sounds crazy...

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.320
but I believe whoever
is calling me is good.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.200
How can you say that?
Look at our kingdom.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.400
I know. It's just that
my magic can feel it.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.040
I can feel it.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.480
-Okay.
-(RUMBLING)

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.160
-(BOTH GASP)
-Oh, no. What now?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.240
KRISTOFF: The Trolls?

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.280
-Kristoff! We missed you!
-Oh!

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.960
Pabbie.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.920
Well, never a dull moment
with you two.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.400
I hope you're prepared
for what you have done, Elsa.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.960
Angry magical spirits are not
for the faint of heart.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.000
Why are they still angry?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.960
What does all of this
have to do with Arendelle?

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.240
Let me see what I can see.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.560
The past is not what it seems.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.240
A wrong demands to be righted.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.280
-Arendelle is not safe.
-(ELSA GASPS)

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.760
The truth must be found.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.040
Without it...

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.400
I see no future.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.640
No future?

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.040
When one can see no future...

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.560
all one can do
is the next right thing.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.200
The next right thing

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:36.880
is for me to go
to the Enchanted Forest...

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.560
and find that voice.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.920
Kristoff, can I borrow
your wagon

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.000
-and Sven?
-SVEN: Hmm?

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.640
I'm not very comfortable
with the idea of that.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.920
-You are not going alone.
-Anna, no.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.480
I have my powers
to protect me. You don't.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.200
Excuse me, I climbed
the North Mountain...

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.280
survived a frozen heart,

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:51.480
and saved you
from my ex-boyfriend...

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.920
and I did it
all without powers,

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.400
-so, you know, I'm coming.
-(INHALES)

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.840
Me, too. I'll drive.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.320
I'll bring the snacks!

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.440
I will look after your people.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.640
Please make sure they stay

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.120
out of the kingdom
until we return.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.760
Of course.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.280
Let's let them know.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.200
Anna, I am worried for her.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.800
We have always feared

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.440
Elsa's powers were too much
for this world.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.000
Now, we must pray
they are enough.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:17.800
(BREATHES SHARPLY)

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.880
I won't let anything
happen to her.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.840
OLAF: Hyah!

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.120
OLAF: Who's into trivia?

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.800
I am. Okay.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.480
Did you know that water
has memory? True fact.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.640
It's disputed by many,
but it's true.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.080
Did you know men are six times

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.640
more likely
to be struck by lightning?

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.920
Did you know gorillas burp
when they're happy?

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.360
Did you know we blink
four million times a day?

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.360
Did you know
wombats poop squares?

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.840
KRISTOFF: Did you know
sleeping quietly

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.640
on long journeys
prevents insanity?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.000
(OLAF CACKLING)

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.440
OLAF: Yeah, that's not true.
KRISTOFF: It is.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.720
ANNA: It's true.
ELSA: Definitely true.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.240
-ANNA: No, it's the truth.
-(SVEN MOANS)

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.720
OLAF: Well,
that was unanimous.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.680
But I will look it up
when we get home.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.120
(OLAF SNORING AND MUMBLING)

00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.840
They're both asleep.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.040
So, what do you wanna do?

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.200
(CHUCKLES)

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.200
Sven, keep us steady, will ya?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.440
(SVEN GRUNTS)

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.840
-Hmm...
-(VOICE CRACKS) Anna. Ahem.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.040
-(IN NORMAL VOICE) Anna?
-Mm-hmm?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.760
Remember
our first trip like this...

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.040
when I said
you'd have to be crazy

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.800
to want to marry
a man you just met?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.480
Wait, what? Crazy?

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.040
You didn't say I was crazy.
You think I'm crazy?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.640
No. I did.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.560
-You were...
-SVEN: Huh? (GRUNTS)

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:27.720
...not crazy.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.080
Clearly. (CHUCKLES)

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.800
Just naive.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.520
Not naive. Just, uh,
new to love. Like I was.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.920
And when you're new,
you're bound to get it wrong.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.960
So you're saying
I'm wrong for you.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.120
What? No, no. I'm not saying

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.640
-you're wrong, or crazy.
-(THE VOICE VOCALIZING)

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.800
-Kristoff, stop. Please.
-Good idea.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.480
I hear it. I hear the voice.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.880
You do?

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:53.800
-Olaf, wake up.
-(OLAF GRUNTS)

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.560
-(SVEN MOANS)
-(ELSA GASPS SOFTLY)

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.480
-Whoa.
-Wow.

